Run from the repository root with migrations/requirements.txt installed.
Forward the lab database: kubectl port-forward svc/postgres 15432:5432

Existing database with the original event_date schema:
  If unversioned, first: alembic stamp 0001
  alembic upgrade 0003
  alembic upgrade 0004        # add scheduled_at
  Deploy A (COALESCE fallback reads); wait for all Events pods to be ready.
  alembic upgrade 0005        # backfill and enforce new NOT NULL
  Deploy B (scheduled_at only); wait for all Events pods to be ready.
  alembic upgrade 0006        # drop old column, retain a date index

Do not upgrade straight to head while old Events code is running.
The committed Events source is Deploy B. Deploy A's three SQL changes and
all transition results are recorded in submissions/lab12.md.

Fresh empty database:
  psql ... -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -f app/seed.sql
  alembic stamp 0006
  alembic current
The final seed includes scheduled_at, nullable email, and the date index.
It already represents 0006, so do not run the old-column migrations on it.
Stamp only after verifying that the seed completed on an empty database.

Rollback order (coordinate writers and readers):
  downgrade to 0005 restores event_date and copies scheduled_at into it;
  deploy compatible fallback code, stop new-only writes or dual-write;
  downgrade to 0004 reconciles old dates and restores the old NOT NULL;
  roll every reader back to the old code before downgrading to 0003.
A one-time copy is not enough if new-only writers continue afterwards.
